Goldstein was also a queen’s pawn, the latter adopting an original defence
which involved the capture of his opponent’s Q.Kt.P. with the queen. The
excursion met with its usual fate, Winter taking advantage of the bad position
of the queen to establish a strong king's side attack and force a win in 30
moves." (Manchester Guardian, 17 November 1927)} 1-0

